    ​[head=3]On Oum Erth[/head]


    While perhaps not the most fundamental part of the gray language, I think it is important to remember WHY you are learning gray. The why can form as great motivation, and losing sight of the why can lead to difficulties in retaining information as time goes on.


    These books, sponsored by NanoTrasen, are focusing on your workplace environment. NanoTrasen wishes you smooth and efficient conversations with your gray coworkers. If you are unable to properly make requests or discuss work matters with your gray coworkers, then that harms productivity!


    So, to meet that end, I will introduce the format the series will take from here: in this chapter, I will introduce the names of work departments found aboard NanoTrasen vessels to you. Then, in subsequent chapters, I will focus on one department and sprinkle in some useful words and phrases! 


    —


