    ​[head=3]Culture Corner[/head]


    One of the highest form of gray artforms is none other than the genre known as “scat.” The name, based on the human artform of vocal improv to act like a musical instrument. The human artform of scatting is difficult, but can create something out of complete and utter nonsense.


    Gray scat is similar, but not entirely the same. This artform is about taking existing language and rearranging it into something else, be it nonsense or coherent. A very common use of it is taking some form of existing human video or audio media and rearranging them into something new.


    It could simply be dialogue or it could form patterns and music! Despite having an incredibly high skill ceiling, this is a very easy to get into artform. As such, it is rather popular on gray forums and social media since all it requires is editing software.


    Recently, gray artists have even begun posting it to NanoTrasen platforms.


    Try searching “SpaceTube Scat” in your NanoTrasen approved browser today!


